++    ; Everything after this point commits the CPU to the 64-bit path:
++    ; WRMSR against IA32_EFER and a far jump into an L-bit segment.
++    ; Neither is defined on a CPU without long mode, and the observed
++    ; behaviour there (qemu-system-i386) is a silent hang right after
++    ; the "entering long mode" banner.  Ask first.  A CPU that answers
++    ; "no" gets a diagnostic on BOTH the serial port and the VGA text
++    ; screen -- the machine this fires on may have no serial cable.
